Changed file: internal/scan/scan.go

Intent:
feat: ffprobe-backed scan metadata + playback-length stream tokens

internal/ffmpeg lands as the FFmpeg boundary leaf (lazy binary resolution per
the architecture map): Probe shells out to ffprobe and parses container,
video codec, and duration. Scan grows a consumer-declared Prober seam wired
from app and the CLI; probe failure (or no FFmpeg) falls back to the old
path-derived metadata, so nothing breaks on bare machines.

Stream tokens now live max(1h, 2x media duration) instead of 5 minutes —
AVPlayer issues range requests against the same URL for the whole runtime,
and revocation/relock are already enforced live per byte request, so the
short expiry only broke playback mid-stream without adding security.

Verified live: scanned MP4 reports probed duration, direct-play token
expires one hour out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

